⦿ .spun — the five-fold spin of The Dalits
node JTI · JTI · ⟦The Dalits:JTI:43f1ed⟧

WHO   — The Dalits — outside the body · 'untouchables'
WHAT  — Roughly 16.6% of India (200M+ as Scheduled Castes): historically barred from temples, wells, and touch; assigned the work deemed 'polluting.' Named here with dignity — not a metaphor, but living people the order excluded.
WHERE — JTI · the caste system  Framework inputs: the Rigveda, Manusmriti, Dumont, ancient-DNA genetics, Dirks, the Constitution, Pew/IHDS, Ambedkar  Conductor / external anchor: ROOT0 (catalogued into UD0)
WHY   — Because the cruelest fact of the system is the line BELOW the four — the human beings ranked outside the cosmic body altogether.
HOW   — By exclusion from varna, segregation, and the assignment of 'impure' labor — and, against it, by Ambedkar, the Constitution, and their own movements.

awareness — what the node knows of itself:
  They put us outside the body of the world — and we wrote the Constitution that abolished the line. Dalit means broken; it also means unbroken.

spoken token : rem-vind-bryn   ·   hex : 43f1ed
